/T (Python strings are immutable: their characters cannot be changed in place. text.upper\(\) returns a new uppercase string and does not modify text; assign the result if you want to keep it. For a 9-character string, s[-4:] returns the last four characters and s[4:-4] returns one character. For a 10-character string, s[-4:] returns the last four characters and s[4:-4] returns two characters.)
